# Sprint 1 Retrospective - ClubEvents

## What Went Well
- Clear Sprint 1 backlog items, acceptance criteria, and story points.
- Active use of branches, Pull Requests, and peer reviews on GitHub.
- Clear core scope covering roles, event CRUD, registration, attendance lists, and AJAX updates.

## What Could Be Improved
- Faster review and merge turnaround for open Pull Requests.
- Clearer distinction between documentation changes and code repository checks.
- Keeping sprint and report notes updated continuously.

## Action Items for Future Sprints
- Complete at least two peer reviews per team member consistently.
- Share new Pull Request links immediately with the team for faster review and merge into `main`.
- Keep sprint notes, client changes, and retrospective items updated for the final 3-5 page report.
